## The mechanism in one line

PowerShell 5.1 funnels every script block, string, and `Add-Type` compilation through `System.Management.Automation.AmsiUtils.ScanContent`, which is a thin P/Invoke wrapper around `AmsiScanBuffer` in `amsi.dll`. Patch the *function* (not the reflection fields) to return `E_INVALIDARG`, and every subsequent scan in the process sees "not initialized → allow." That survives the 2024–2025 field-name and string-signature hardening because it never touches `AmsiUtils` internals at all.

